course: dictionary
lesson: 13112
title: Bending a joint
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your body moves at its joints, the places where two bones meet. Flexion is the word for bending a joint, so the angle between the bones gets smaller. When you bend your elbow to lift a cup, you are making flexion happen.
explain: The opposite of flexion is extension, which means straightening the joint again. When you bend your knee and then straighten it, you do flexion and then extension. Scientists and doctors often say «flexion and extension» together.
explain: Flexion is a noun, the name of the movement itself. In a PE or science lesson, you might be asked to show knee flexion or to name the joint that is doing the bending.
fact: Flexion means bending a joint so that the angle between its bones gets smaller.
fact: «Knee flexion» means bending your knee.
fact: The biceps muscle causes flexion of the elbow, and the triceps causes extension.
fact: Physiotherapists measure flexion after an injury to see how far a joint can still bend.
fact: In grammar, flexion (more often called inflection) means changing a word's ending to show its grammar.
exercise: When you bend your elbow to lift a cup, what is happening? | Your elbow is cold | Extension of the elbow | *Flexion of the elbow | Your elbow is growing
exercise: «Knee flexion» means what? | Straightening your knee | *Bending your knee | Shaking your knee | Hitting your knee
exercise: Which word is the opposite of flexion? | Bone | *Extension | Angle | Injury
test: After an injury, a physiotherapist measures flexion. What is she checking? | What colour the skin is | *How far the joint can bend | How fast you can run | How long the bone is
test: Which two words are the movements that a joint can make? | Extension and sleep | Bone and muscle | Flexion and growth | *Flexion and extension
exam: Which sentence describes flexion? | *Bending your arm at the elbow so the angle gets smaller | Straightening your arm fully | Breathing in deeply | Closing your eyes tightly
